{
  "$schema": "../family.schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "farmer-carry",
  "name": "Farmer Carry",
  "definition": "A duration-tracked bilateral carry in which equal side loading creates a continuous tendency to open both hands while the athlete walks forward on a level surface with the upper arms at the sides, neutral humeral and forearm rotation, the elbows held extended, and no grip assistance. The roster owns paired dumbbells and Lockie and Lazar's exact conventional closed dual-height hex frame carried from its high handles. The trap-bar pickup is setup rather than a credited deadlift repetition, and the product maps the source's distance task to duration tracking. The sagittal family plane is grounded in resisted hand.fingerExtension; ordinary gait remains locomotor substrate rather than training-defining prime actions. Loaded-grip and support roles not directly measured for the trap bar are transparent carry-mechanics transfers. Holds, suitcase carriage, marching in place, backward or turning paths, uneven loads, straps, low or arbitrary trap-bar handles, open frames, rack, overhead, front-loaded, yoke, and lunge variants remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb",
    "christophy-2012-lumbar-spine",
    "gaffney-2014-trapezius-subdivisions",
    "holzbaur-2005-upper-extremity",
